{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":5,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1480168772,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOkxhYmVsZWRFdmVudDg3MjYxMjQxNw=="},"added":["conference agenda item"],"removed":[]},{"type":5,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1480171974,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOkxhYmVsZWRFdmVudDg3MjYyMTc5Nw=="},"added":["annex-v6/7"],"removed":[]},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1480184286,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI2MzA3Nzg4Mw==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1143#issuecomment-263077883"},"message":"I am increasingly under the impression that we should ship v6 repos in unlocked state from datasets.datalad.org.\n\nFTR: https://git-annex.branchable.com/forum/converting_a_v5_repo_to_an_always_unlocked_v6_repo/\n\nAt the same time we need to expose `annex.thin` via `install`.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1480185453,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI2MzA3ODgwOQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1143#issuecomment-263078809"},"message":"FTR: In v6 unlocked repo mode (and in any direct mode repository too!), we need to run:\n\n````\ngit annex sync --no-push --no-pull\n````\n\nbefore we perform any checks on whether \"master\" is of a particular state. The above command syncs all potential changes in the \"adjusted\" (or \"annex/direct/....\" branch into the actual master -- without talking to remotes.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1480265885,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI2MzEzMzMwMQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1143#issuecomment-263133301"},"message":"Still playing with it to get some real life impression. I am doing this (https://git-annex.branchable.com/forum/converting_a_v5_repo_to_an_always_unlocked_v6_repo/) with a single repo (40k files with some 700GB of data). The `sync` part is taking ages. It passes all files individually through the clean smudge filter on commit -- we are talking hours of runtime.\n\nHere is an impression of the commands running during the commit stage:\n\n````\ngit-annex smudge --clean 'SOMEFILE'\ngit --git-dir=.git --work-tree=. --literal-pathspecs check-attr -z --stdin annex.backend annex.numcopies annex.largefiles --\ngit --git-dir=.git --work-tree=. --literal-pathspecs cat-file --batch\ngit --git-dir=.git --work-tree=. --literal-pathspecs cat-file --batch-check=%(objectname) %(objecttype) %(objectsize)\n````","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1480269991,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI2MzEzNjk2MQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1143#issuecomment-263136961"},"message":"Iirc 40k files is already a notable burden even for regular git  manipulations\n-- \nSent from a phone which beats iPhone.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1480270107,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI2MzEzNzA1Nw==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1143#issuecomment-263137057"},"message":"On November 26, 2016 1:18:06 PM EST, Michael Hanke \u003cnotifications@github.com\u003e wrote:\n\u003eI am increasingly under the impression that we should ship v6 repos in\n\u003eunlocked state from datasets.datalad.org.\n\u003e\n\u003eFTR:\n\u003ehttps://git-annex.branchable.com/forum/converting_a_v5_repo_to_an_always_unlocked_v6_repo/\n\u003e\n\u003eAt the same time we need to expose `annex.thin` via `install`.\n\u003e\n\u003e\n\u003e-- \n\u003eYou are receiving this because you are subscribed to this thread.\n\u003eReply to this email directly or view it on GitHub:\n\u003ehttps://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1143#issuecomment-263077883\n\nI thought that the annex format we store them on remote could be different from the local clones... Was I wrong?\n-- \nSent from a phone which beats iPhone.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1480271596,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI2MzEzODQyMg==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1143#issuecomment-263138422"},"message":"\u003e I thought that the annex format we store them on remote could be different from the local clones... Was I wrong?\n\nIf you are thinking repository indirect vs direct mode for sure. In v6 it is possible to actually commit whether a single file is locked or unlocked. I have yet to fully explore how much of that is propagated to remotes under what conditions. But in any case, for clones from datasets.d.o it is somewhat less important to protect files from getting lost/modified. Any such change is easily recovered from by reobtaining the necessary version. Going unlocked by default also addresses the \"my file browser is lost in the annex store\" problem.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1480482763,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI2Mzc4NDk0OA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1143#issuecomment-263784948"},"message":"Git 2.11 is out with multifile smudge filtering. This should bring a major speedup for v6.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1480768842,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI2NDYzNzA0Nw==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1143#issuecomment-264637047"},"message":"Re discussion: here is the quote on mixing locked and unlocked files in a single repo:\n\n\u003e mixing locked and unlocked files\n\u003e A v6 repository can contain both locked and unlocked files. You can switch a file back and forth using the git annex lock and git annex unlock commands. This changes what's stored in git between a git-annex symlink (locked) and a git-annex pointer file (unlocked). To add a file to the repository in locked mode, use git annex add; to add a file in unlocked mode, use git add.\n\u003e If you want to mostly keep files locked, but be able to locally switch to having them all unlocked, you can do so using git annex adjust --unlock. See git-annex-adjust for details. This is particularly useful when using filesystems like FAT, and OS's like Windows that don't support symlinks.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1520528786,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM3MTU1MzYwNg==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1143#issuecomment-371553606"},"message":"I think we could postpone this utopian idea for now","files":null},{"type":4,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1520528786,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDExOkNsb3NlZEV2ZW50MTUxMTU5NTk5Mg=="},"status":2},{"type":5,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1537378371,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDE0OlVubGFiZWxlZEV2ZW50MTg1NTY4NDcxOA=="},"added":[],"removed":["conference agenda item"]}]}